\title{hcbic: How Much Data Does It Take to Test an Expert Causal Diagram?}
\description{
Tools to ask how well data can support or contradict an expert-elicited causal diagram (a directed acyclic graph) of a farm system. The package holds one expert diagram of agroforestry and livelihoods, simulates data from it, runs hill-climbing structure learning scored by the Bayesian information criterion (BIC), and reports how many observations are needed to recover the diagram and to detect each missing arc.
